      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "content": "$\\text{base} + \\text{height} + \\text{third side}$",
        "rationale": "Adding the sides gives the perimeter, not the area."
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Area of a triangle $= \\frac{1}{2}bh$, where $h$ is the perpendicular height from the base to the opposite vertex.",
